  "id": "COMPOUND:41664 - PROTEIN:3941",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Cytisine, N-formyl- and Alpha-actinin-1, mediated through the compound 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol. This compound is identified as a target of both Cytisine, N-formyl- and Alpha-actinin-1, with multiple pathways linking the two entities. Pathway 1 and 2 both indicate that Cytisine, N-formyl- targets HCT-8, which in turn is targeted by 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, which ultimately targets Alpha-actinin-1. Pathway 3 also shows that Cytisine, N-formyl- targets HCT-8, which is targeted by another compound, and this same compound targets Alpha-actinin-1. The evidence suggests a common pathway where Cytisine, N-formyl- may influence the activity of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, which then affects Alpha-actinin-1. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the different pathways, with scores ranging from 0.6906 to 0.7057, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanisms appear to involve the compound 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol as a central mediator, linking Cytisine, N-formyl- to Alpha-actinin-1 through its interaction with HCT-8.",
